       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg PO three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual limits:\n\n- **Daily maximum:** 4,000 mg/day for adults. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 1,000 mg. Some protocols allow up to 1,000 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Risk:** At 6 g/day, hepatotoxicity is a serious concern, even with normal liver function. At 70 kg, that's about 86 mg/kg/day, and the usual ceiling is about 75 mg/kg/day.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some common alternatives:\n\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours\n\nIf you want the 2000 mg TID dose for a reason I'm missing, please confirm it explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting the intent. Otherwise, tell me which of the corrected doses you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
